# ── Never commit this ────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC. .env holds DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY, the only thing
# that can decrypt the credentials Sparta issues to agents. It is
# generated on the customer's own host by setup.sh and must never
# exist here in any form.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Release archives are built by CI and attached to a GitHub Release.
# They are never committed -- a committed tarball is a second copy of
# the release that can silently drift from the tagged one.
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip

# Certificates and keys. Nothing in this repo should ever hold one,
# so these entries exist to make an accident inert rather than to
# cover an expected case.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12

# Local artifacts
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
